## 5. WIP=1 and Verified Completion Rate

- Only one br issue `in_progress` at a time — mechanically enforced
  natively by `br` via the `in_progress` capacity cap in
  `.beads/policy.yaml` (`hard: 1`), which rejects a second `br update
  --claim` while one is already claimed.
- Verified Completion Rate (VCR) = closed-with-passing-verification /
  claimed. If you claim an issue and can't get it to a real
  Definition-of-Done pass, don't claim the next one. Report the blocker
  (label it `human` — `br update <id> --labels human`, then `br list
  --label human` surfaces it — or a comment) instead of moving on.

---

## 6. Clean State / Session-Close Checklist

Beyond `br`'s own workflow (see AGENTS.md's beads-workflow section from
`br agents --add`), before ending a session that touched code:

- [ ] `git status` clean or changes are staged with a clear reason to leave them uncommitted
- [ ] {{TEST_COMMAND}} passes (once scaffolded) — `.claude/hooks/stop-gate.sh` blocks Stop otherwise
- [ ] br issue status matches reality (`in_progress` only if genuinely still being worked; closed issues have a real `--reason`)
- [ ] Any new architecture decision is recorded in `DECISIONS.md`, not left implicit
- [ ] Next session's starting point is discoverable via `br ready` alone — no tribal knowledge required
